tive Government of the United Kingdom.\" That indicates John Major was PM before 1997, and his resignation as leader. But we need evidence that Margaret Thatcher was succeeded by John Major in 1990. Not present.\n\nWe have evidence: \"These were the first annual local elections for the new Conservative Prime Minister Margaret Thatcher.\" That indicates Thatcher was PM in 1980. Not about succession.\n\nWe have evidence about \"The Conservative Party, officially ... is a centre-right political party...\" not about succession.\n\nThus we may not have direct evidence for the answer. Could answer \"noanswer\". But maybe we can infer from evidence: John Major succeeded Margaret Thatcher as PM in 1990. Is there any sentence referencing that? Not in given evidence. There's no mention of Thatcher's resignation or Major's succession. So cannot verify.\n\nThus answer noanswer.\n\nWe need JSON with answer \"noanswer\" and empty citations list."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1716,"completion_tokens":575,"total_tokens":2291,"audio_prompt_tokens":0},"created":1791963225,"object":"chat.completion","prompt_filter_results":null}